🔥JIT :
JIT (Just-In-Time) Compilation is a runtime optimization technique where code is compiled into
native machine code while the application is running, instead of before execution.

  Kotlin/Java
        │
        ▼
    .class
        │
        ▼
    DEX (.dex)
        │
        ▼
   Installed
        │
        ▼
Android Runtime (ART) (observe most  frequent method)
        │
        ▼
JIT compiles frequently executed methods into native code
        │
        ▼
CPU executes native machine code


🔥What is AOT (Ahead-Of-Time) Compilation?
AOT (Ahead-Of-Time) Compilation is a compilation technique where bytecode is compiled into native machine code before the application runs, instead of during execution.
In Android, AOT is performed by the Android Runtime (ART) during app installation or while the device is idle



