🔥What is the Looper, Handler, and MessageQueue?
Looper ->
A Thread can have at most one Looper associated with it.
A Looper continuously checks a thread's MessageQueue and processes messages one by one until the Looper quits or the process/thread terminates.
For example, Android's main thread uses a Looper to process UI events, callbacks, and posted tasks.

MessageQueue->
The Looper owns a MessageQueue

Handler->
posts work to a thread's MessageQueue.

🔹flow:

Button Click
      │
      ▼
Handler.post()
      │
      ▼
Creates a Message
      │
      ▼
MessageQueue
      │
      ▼
Looper picks the message
      │
      ▼
Runs Runnable
      │
      ▼
textView.setText("Clicked")

